      "category": "nodal",
      "source": {
        "text": "Mansagari",
        "chapter": "4",
        "note": "All seven classical grahas between Rahu and Ketu, none on the axis, on either side; B.V. Raman's Hindu Predictive Astrology reads it the same way. Not read at rank 1: the recording engine computes it in code and cites Mansagari, and this rule says the same thing in the language. The engine names the nodes alone as the graha involved; this rule names the seven it caught. No verse for it was found in BPHS, Brihat Jataka, Saravali, Phaladeepika, Jataka Parijata or Kalaprakasika: it is a modern construction, and its rank says so.",
        "rank": 3
      },
      "conditions": [
